{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 exit — confirmed root cause (analysis only)\n\n### Problem and measurement result\n\nA fresh, unfiltered, single-branch clone reproduces the report at tickets tip `2fd4a1a62c92f534825097153dd1767e97ec4b47`; this is not a stale-local-clone artifact.\n\n| Layer | Exact result |\n|---|---:|\n| Reachable Git pack | 322.57 MiB (535,779 objects, one pack) |\n| `.git` logical size | 358,767,066 B |\n| Checked-out tree logical | 827,550,463 B (789.21 MiB) |\n| Checked-out tree 4-KiB allocated | 1,116,577,792 B (1.040 GiB) |\n| Tree block slack | 289,027,329 B |\n| Whole fresh clone logical / allocated | 1,186,317,529 B / 1,475,424,256 B |\n\nThe tree has 112,788 files. Of them, 89,577 (79.42%) are at most 4 KiB: they hold 132,902,547 logical bytes but allocate 366,903,296 bytes. Those files contribute 234,000,749 bytes, or 81% of all block slack. Thus the checked-out tree exceeds 1 GiB physically even though its logical payload is only 789.21 MiB. The Git branch pack itself is not over 1 GiB.\n\nCurrent tree attribution, logical / 4-KiB allocated bytes:\n\n- retired snapshots: 254,853,040 / 258,666,496\n- review results: 238,486,830 / 255,561,728\n- other retired events: 127,483,175 / 239,804,416\n- active snapshots: 95,128,343 / 108,331,008\n- enrichment lifecycle: 71,921,418 / 198,225,920\n- other: 25,559,514 / 41,857,024\n- `.bridge_state`: 14,118,143 / 14,131,200\n\n### Proven anomalous-data mechanism\n\nExactly three tickets dominate the abnormal payload:\n\n- `undyed-high-kiwi` (`8625-7bea-67db-4cdc`): 174,969,874 B\n- `icicled-unstable-urial` (`9305-b42c-3262-4c58`): 69,311,996 B\n- `weary-wavy-hen` (`e27c-5a20-cd13-43b2`): 28,633,659 B\n\nSix large bodies were imported repeatedly under distinct Jira comment IDs. Conservative exact attribution is 760 excess COMMENT files / 18,496,834 B plus 229,222,450 repeated body bytes embedded in snapshots (17,164,261 active; 212,058,189 retired): 247,719,284 B total. That is 29.93% of the whole logical tree, 46.14% of logical growth since the rewrite, and 90.77% of those three directories. Recurring snapshots amplify the raw duplicate-event bytes by about 13.4x.\n\nThe execution chain is confirmed:\n\n1. Commit `27b868ba55eb5f699d3c4b0b72891aaeb969eef3`, ticket `emersed-specific-mutt` (`789c-1251-fc21-4cf6`), introduced the persistent comment-ID map but assumed every successful `add_comment` returned a top-level `{\"id\": ...}`. The story description states that exact contract. Cloud ACLI actually returns a batch envelope with no created-comment ID; historical `_record_comment_id` silently returned, leaving production `comment_ids` empty. Runtime proof and elimination of the other guards are recorded on `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker` (`aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615`). Current repair code documents the transport asymmetry at `dispatch_apply_phases.py:311-352`.\n2. With the primary mapped-key guard inert, only lossy body equality remained. Rich ADF/wiki round-tripping changed bodies, so the secondary test at `outbound_comments.py:671-725` re-posted them each pass.\n3. Oversized outbound comments were decorated and then right-truncated, cutting off the trailing reconciler marker. That necessary historical condition is documented/fixed by `unreal-empathetic-illadopsis` (`5931-78a3-95d2-44cd`) and `outbound_comments.py:227-305`.\n4. Inbound sync filters marker-bearing echoes, then deduplicates by Jira ID, not body (`inbound_collection_diffs.py:97-166`). Each re-post had a distinct Jira ID, so every markerless copy became a distinct local COMMENT event (`apply_inbound_events.py:516-537`).\n5. Compaction writes the complete reduced ticket state into each new SNAPSHOT, renames every folded event and prior snapshot to `.retired`, and retains them permanently (`compact_txn.py:266-322,470-545`; `docs/concurrency.md:61-67`). On the largest ticket, retained snapshots progress from 28 comments / 600,873 B shortly after the introducing change to 388 comments / 8,730,955 B; the active 394-comment snapshot is 10,082,163 B. This directly confirms snapshot size follows compiled comment count.\n\n### Why the physical threshold was crossed now\n\nThe duplicate-comment/snapshot chain is the largest abnormal retained payload, but it is not by itself the instant of threshold crossing. Allocated tree size was:\n\n- Aug 20: 904,732,672 B\n- Aug 21: 983,625,728 B\n- Aug 22: 1,051,222,016 B (over decimal 1 GB)\n- Aug 23: 1,116,577,792 B (over 1 GiB)\n\nFrom Aug 21 through Aug 23, merge-safe enrichment retention added 34,289 files, 55,297,265 logical bytes, and 140,500,992 allocated bytes. This small-file burst pushed the already-bloated tree across the physical boundary. Current enrichment lifecycle residence is 48,372 files / 71,921,418 logical B / 198,225,920 allocated B. Physical pruning was deliberately removed by commit `be8a0c059571b340cd7705191769a4a64998643d`, because deleting committed UUID events breaks stale-clone union reconvergence. The separate retry bug fixed by `spongy-illjudged-terrier` (`569c-931f-69a2-4c1d`) contributed hundreds of unnecessary claims, but does not explain most of the 34,289-file burst.\n\nTherefore the parsimonious threshold account is composite: historical comment echoes created the largest abnormal logical payload; full-state snapshots plus permanent retirement multiplied and preserved it; intentional enrichment lifecycle retention plus 4-KiB block rounding supplied the immediate physical threshold crossing.\n\n### Prior rewrite and current fixes\n\nThe prior history reclaim remains effective on the layer it actually rewrote. Baseline `1300f383c75b10231fbd814cb9f6a1dfa269a26e` had 39,142 files, 290,690,203 logical tree bytes, 396,152,832 allocated tree bytes, 68,920 commits, and 4,663 merges. Current content is newly reachable post-rewrite material. `git fsck --full --unreachable --no-reflogs` is empty; the fresh clone has only local/remote tickets refs at one tip; the pre-rewrite tip is absent. The rewrite deliberately restored an identical HEAD tree and removed historical `.bridge_state` versions, so its <=150 MiB acceptance measured pack size, not checkout or whole-clone footprint.\n\nThe comment defects are also fixed, but fixes do not retroactively delete committed artifacts. Fix `8d98c298fa816acf51b1bae069f36695066b2695` is deployed; current `bindings.json` has 790 comment-map entries. The first resumed pass posted the previously unmapped backlog once, the next imported remaining echoes, and the third reported `with_comments=0` / `Reconcile converged.` No later exact-body duplicate COMMENT event exists through the frozen tip. Marker-preservation fix `6724e79e8ff857b54dd36a62006a89445fc10ad6` is also deployed.\n\n### Rival hypotheses rejected or bounded\n\n- **Old unreachable history / ref pins / failed rewrite:** rejected by the fresh-clone reproduction, single-tip ref set, empty unreachable fsck, and absent old tip.\n- **High commit count alone:** contributing only to `.git`, not the checkout. Packed commit objects occupy 27,548,070 B and trees 60,149,990 B. Commit objects cannot enlarge the checked-out tree.\n- **Whole-file duplication defeating Git blob identity:** rejected. Only 128 identical 21-byte tombstones exist (2,667 excess logical bytes). The repeated payload is inside structurally distinct signed events/snapshots; delta compression is why the pack is much smaller than the checkout.\n- **Review results as the new anomaly:** large retained baseline, not the sudden mechanism. They occupy 238,486,830 B now, but about 170.3 MB already existed at the rewrite baseline.\n- **Renewed old `.bridge_state` cache churn:** rejected as checkout cause. Current `.bridge_state` is 14.1 MB; `bindings.json` has zero `baseline_advanced_at` and zero inline `last_get_pass` fields. Separate peer-confirmation no-op rewrites are real but the path-specific cost is 6,077,416 packed bytes, not the 1-GiB tree; corrected on `proposed-kitschy-firefly`.\n- **Current recurrence of the comment loop:** rejected by deployed ancestry, the three-pass convergence sequence, 790 mapped comments, and absence of later duplicate events.\n\n### Legitimacy, origin, and disposition\n\nThe comment-map behavior is a confirmed `defect`: it violates `emersed-specific-mutt`'s explicit append-once acceptance criteria and existing map-persistence tests. The attributed origin is commit `27b868ba55...` / `emersed-specific-mutt` (`789c-1251-fc21-4cf6`), classified `plan_defect`: its central transport-contract assumption was false. The marker-loss condition came through the untrailered standalone-rebar import `b534f47a7f9...`; no earlier project ticket/proven introducing change is available, so that necessary secondary origin is explicitly unattributable/preexisting rather than guessed.\n\nNo Phase 2 repair was authorized or performed in this ticket. Existing repairs are deployed; remaining work is safe reclamation and growth control:\n\n- `irongray-unlucky-discus` (`93c4-2b9f-749a-4243`): safe targeted reclaim of the proven duplicate comments/snapshots.\n- `epidemic-chocolaty-imago` (`0754-cfc5-e451-4e9b`): whole-store budgets for pack, logical tree, allocated tree, file count/slack, and total clone.\n- `apparent-sighted-cockatoo` (`4520-11a6-7458-454f`): merge-safe enrichment retention/archival design.\n- `polite-antivirus-bedbug` (`536b-8930-b922-4063`): `.retired` GC after a real causal-stability model exists.\n- `proposed-kitschy-firefly` (`266c-394a-9e6f-4c2e`): bound peer-confirmation sidecar churn (measurement corrected to 6,077,416 packed bytes for that path).\n\nConclusion: the prior cache-history rewrite and reconciler fixes worked, but they addressed different layers and did not erase retained ticket artifacts. The current >1-GiB physical tree is explained by a proven historical comment-echo payload amplified by snapshot retention, then pushed over the boundary by enrichment small files and block slack."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787523836585350001,"uuid":"483b9359-3ce6-46dd-8dc5-f4041963dcc9"}